= S * np.exp(-q * T) * norm.cdf(d1) - K * np.exp(-r * T) * norm.cdf(d2)\n    return call_price","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T16:39:17.555971Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T16:39:17.556305Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T16:39:17.563014Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-29T16:39:17.556275Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T16:39:17.561671Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":16},{"cell_type":"code","source":"q = ticker.info.get('dividendYield', 0.0)\nprint(\"AAPL dividend yield:\", q)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T16:39:19.192215Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T16:39:19.192547Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T16:39:19.198583Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-29T16:39:19.192518Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T16:39:19.197684Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"AAPL dividend yield: 0.32\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":17},{"cell_type":"code","source":"S = 330.78\nK = 330.0\nT = 31 / 365\nr = 0.04\nq = 0.32 / 100\nsigma = 0.2924\n\nprice_div = black_scholes_call_div(S, K, T, r, q, sigma)\nprint(\"Black-Scholes (dividend-adjusted) price:\", price_div)\nprint(\"Black-Scholes (no dividend) price:\", price)   # from your earlier cell\nprint(\"Actual market price (midpoint):\", 11.60)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T16:42:41.187608Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T16:42:41.18802Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T16:42:41.19513Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-29T16:42:41.187985Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T16:42:41.194226Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Black-Scholes (dividend-adjusted) price: 12.135701225137979\nBlack-Scholes (no dividend) price: 12.184531142638036\nActual market price (midpoint): 11.6\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":22},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Implied Volatility Solver\n\nBlack-Scholes normally goes (volatility → price). We need t